## Process

### Phase 1: Prerequisites

The interpreter version has ONE source of truth: `.python-version`. Do not
hardcode versions anywhere; run `env_probe.py pins` or read the pin.

| Tool | Floor | Verify |
|------|-------|--------|
| uv | Must resolve the `.python-version` pin (old container uv builds cannot; reinstall via the astral.sh standalone installer, never `uv self update`, which hits GitHub API rate limits on shared egress IPs) | `uv python list "$(cat .python-version)"` prints a row |
| Python | Exactly the `.python-version` pin, installed by uv | `python3 --version` |
| Node.js | The `NODE_MAJOR` value in `scripts/bootstrap-vm.sh` (AGENTS.md floor says "Node LTS") | `node --version` |
| PowerShell | 7.5.4+ per AGENTS.md Stack. Note: zero `.ps1` files remain in the repo (ADR-042 Python migration), so pwsh is rarely exercised, but the floor is still declared | `pwsh --version` |
| gh CLI | 2.60+ per AGENTS.md Stack | `gh --version` |
| git, jq, curl | any recent | `git --version` |

Container or VM setup: `bash scripts/bootstrap-vm.sh` automates all of the above
on Ubuntu (needs sudo; export `GH_TOKEN` first). It installs uv, the pinned
Python via `uv python install --default`, Node 22, pwsh, gh, syncs dependencies,
and installs Lefthook. Do not copy its shell implementation for new scripts;
ADR-042 requires Python for new automation.

Manual Python install when not using the bootstrap script:

```bash
uv python install --default "$(cat .python-version)"
```

### Phase 2: Core Install

From the repo root:

```bash
uv sync --frozen --extra dev
uv run --frozen lefthook install --reset-hooks-path
uv run --frozen lefthook check-install
```

What these do:

- `uv sync --frozen --extra dev` builds `.venv/` from `uv.lock` exactly as
  locked (`--frozen` never rewrites the lockfile) with dev extras. The pre-push
  gate runs validation through `uv run --frozen`, so this `.venv` is the
  environment a push validates against (`grep -n "uv sync --frozen" scripts/bootstrap-vm.sh`).
- `lefthook install` installs Git shims for the events in `lefthook.yml`.
  `check-install` verifies that the shims are active. Lefthook reads the
  configuration at runtime, so editing the jobs under an already-installed hook
  type needs no reinstall. Adding or removing a hook type does: with
  `no_auto_install: true` set, the new type has no shim until install runs
  again.

### Phase 3: Verify the Install

Run the smoke probe. It runs `lefthook version`, `lefthook check-install`, and
`pytest tests/test_paths.py --collect-only`, and compares the lefthook version
to the `lefthook==` pin in `pyproject.toml`.

```bash
python3 "${COPILOT_PLUGIN_ROOT:-${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT:-.claude}}/skills/ai-agents-build-and-env/scripts/env_probe.py" --repo . smoke
```

Exit 0 means all three passed. Exit 1 names the failing command. Exit 3 means
`uv` is missing. It does not check PyYAML or the interpreter: use `pins` for the
pin values, then `uv run python -c "import yaml; print(yaml.__version__)"` and
`python3 --version` to compare.

### Phase 4: MCP Layer

`.mcp.json` at repo root defines two servers. Copy `.env.example` to `.env`
and fill keys (`env_probe.py envfile` lists the key names in `.env.example`). Never commit
`.env` (universal.md MUST 6: no secrets).

{{> no-secrets}}

| Server | Transport | Role | When absent |
|--------|-----------|------|-------------|
| serena | stdio, `uvx --from git+https://github.com/oraios/serena` (port 24282, context claude-code) | Canonical memory (ADR-106) plus LSP symbol navigation | Memories stay readable as plain files under `.serena/memories/` (`env_probe.py pins` reports the entry count). The LSP read gate that could misfire on code files was retired |
| deepwiki | http, `https://mcp.deepwiki.com/mcp` | External GitHub repo documentation | No local impact; fall back to web search |

Proxy and TLS note (generic, not environment-specific): the stdio server is
fetched by `uvx` on first launch, so a corporate proxy must allow uv's
downloads and uv must trust the proxy CA. Use standard `HTTPS_PROXY` plus uv's
system-certificate option (`UV_SYSTEM_CERTS`; the older `UV_NATIVE_TLS` name is
deprecated as of uv 0.11.26). Never disable TLS verification.

### Phase 5: Editor and LSP Reality

This repo prefers LSP-first navigation (ADR-062, `.claude/rules/lsp-first.md`):
use Serena symbol tools over grep for code navigation. This is static steering
now, not a runtime gate. The PreToolUse LSP gate and its environment escapes
(`SKIP_LSP_GATE`, `LSP_GATE_MODE`, `LSP_DOWN`) were retired; no Read
call is blocked and there is nothing to set.

## Known Traps

Each row verified 2026-10-31. Longer stories live with the sibling skills
`ai-agents-failure-archaeology` and `ai-agents-debugging-playbook`.

| Trap | Symptom | Fix |
|------|---------|-----|
| CONTRIBUTING.md build commands were DEAD before commit b320f4ac1 | CONTRIBUTING.md said `build/Generate-Agents.ps1` PowerShell invocation until commit b320f4ac1 repointed it to `build/generate_agents.py` (`git show b320f4ac1 -- CONTRIBUTING.md`); zero `.ps1` files exist in the repo (ADR-042) | Real commands: `uv run python build/generate_agents.py` and `uv run python build/scripts/build_all.py` |
| PEP 668: bare pip fails | `pip install X` errors with externally-managed-environment on uv-managed interpreters | Everything goes through uv: `uv sync`, `uv add`, `uv run` (`grep -n "uv sync --frozen" scripts/bootstrap-vm.sh`) |
| Skill scripts need the project venv | `.claude/skills/github/scripts/pr/*.py` import `github_core`, which imports `yaml` at load; bare `python3` throws `ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'yaml'` unless `.venv/bin` is first on PATH (bootstrap-vm.sh arranges that; a manual setup usually does not) | Run skill scripts with `uv run python`, which resolves the venv deterministically |
| Moving a worktree leaves the uv shebangs stale | Direct `.venv/bin/pytest` fails with "bad interpreter" after `mv`; the shebangs in `.venv/bin/*` (POSIX) or `.venv/Scripts/*` (Windows) still name the old worktree path | Run `scripts/maintenance/repair_worktree_venv.py` with `uv run python` (or `uv sync --frozen --extra dev --reinstall`: `--reinstall` recreates the launchers a bare `--frozen` sync would leave stale, `--extra dev` keeps pytest/ruff/mypy, `--frozen` matches CI); prefer `uv run python -m pytest` for move-safe validation. Detect without mutating: `instruments.py run venv-stale-check` (exit 1 means stale) |
| Two floors, not one | `pyproject.toml project.requires-python` says `requires-python = ">=3.14"` (the dev/install contract), but plugin hooks run under the host's ambient interpreter, which may be older | Develop and test against `.python-version`. The blocking CI syntax gate parses every file at the hook-portability floor (`syntax_floor` in `env_probe.py pins`), NOT the dev pin, so hooks stay portable to older hosts (decoupled from `requires-python`); see `ai-agents-debugging-playbook` |
| LF line endings enforced | CRLF in YAML frontmatter breaks the Copilot CLI parser (github/copilot-cli#694); `.gitattributes:59` sets `* text=auto eol=lf` | Configure your editor for LF; never commit CRLF |
| Pre-push jobs can take minutes | Lefthook runs the named validators in `lefthook.yml` for matching push files | Budget minutes per push; do not attempt `--no-verify` (prohibited, AGENTS.md Never list) |
| Skill test location | Skill tests live in `tests/skills/NAME/`, never inside the skill directory | the colocated-test guard blocks test files placed inside a skill; details in `ai-agents-validation-and-qa` |

## Verification

The 15-minute smoke checklist. All boxes checked means the environment works.

- [ ] `env_probe.py smoke` exits 0 (lefthook version, check-install, test_paths collection)
- [ ] `uv run python -c "import yaml"` exits silently (venv has project deps)
- [ ] `uv run ruff --version` prints a version
- [ ] `python3 --version` matches `cat .python-version`
- [ ] `node --version` major matches `env_probe.py pins` `node_major`; `gh --version` prints 2.60+; `pwsh --version` prints 7.5+
- [ ] `.env` exists locally (copied from `.env.example`) and is NOT tracked: `env_probe.py envfile` reports `tracked_env: false`
- [ ] Optional, requires network: the Serena MCP server starts (harness lists `mcp__serena__*` tools); if not, confirm the ADR-007 fallbacks (superseded by ADR-106; the degradation rule is not restated there) in Phase 4 before proceeding

## Scripts

Run these instead of counting or comparing by hand. Each is read-only.

```bash
python3 "${COPILOT_PLUGIN_ROOT:-${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT:-.claude}}/skills/ai-agents-build-and-env/scripts/env_probe.py" --repo . pins      # interpreter, lefthook, PyYAML, requires-python, Node major, syntax floor, memory entries
python3 "${COPILOT_PLUGIN_ROOT:-${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT:-.claude}}/skills/ai-agents-build-and-env/scripts/env_probe.py" --repo . envfile   # .env present, .env tracked (exit 1), .env.example keys
python3 "${COPILOT_PLUGIN_ROOT:-${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT:-.claude}}/skills/ai-agents-build-and-env/scripts/env_probe.py" --repo . smoke     # Phase 3 commands (needs uv)
python3 "${COPILOT_PLUGIN_ROOT:-${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT:-.claude}}/skills/ai-agents-build-and-env/scripts/instruments.py" --repo . list
```

`pins` answers what the files say, not what is installed: compare with
`python3 --version` and `node --version` yourself. `envfile` cannot tell whether a key
value is valid. `instruments.py list` also links the stale-launcher check
`scripts/maintenance/repair_worktree_venv.py --check`, which only covers a
worktree whose `.venv` exists.

## Anti-Patterns

- Following CONTRIBUTING.md or templates/README.md build instructions. They
  predate ADR-042; the pwsh commands cannot run.
- `pip install` anything, or `uv pip install` into the interpreter. PEP 668
  blocks it; the venv from `uv sync --frozen --extra dev` is the environment.
- Pushing with `--no-verify` or recreating a skip flag for the pre-push hook.
  Escape hatches here get teeth or get abused (session 1187); skipping hooks is
  on the AGENTS.md Never list.
- Committing `.env`, or putting keys anywhere but env vars (universal.md MUST 6).
- Editing files with a CRLF editor profile. One CRLF save can break Copilot CLI
  YAML frontmatter parsing downstream.
- Treating a missing MCP server as a blocker. ADR-007 (superseded by ADR-106; the degradation rule is not restated there) mandates graceful
  degradation: fall back per the Phase 4 table and keep working.
- Hand-fixing `.venv` contents or relying on whatever system `python3` happens
  to resolve to. Re-run `uv sync --frozen --extra dev` instead.

